{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:v120-reviewer-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:58cd55a6683253e967dd", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report declares the complete planned set of 40 nest boxes as the scientific target.", "observed_value": "40 planned units declared as target", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "The declared scientific target is the complete planned set of 40 monitored nest boxes."}]}, {"description": "The selected result uses the complete planned set of 40 as the denominator, and 24/40 = 60.0 percent, which matches the reported rate exactly. The computation therefore uses the complete declared domain, not the retained subset (24/32 would be 75.0 percent, which is not what is reported).", "observed_value": "24/40 = 60.0 percent, matching the reported figure", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Confirmed fledging events occurred in 24 of the 40 planned nest boxes, a fledging-event rate of 60.0 percent of the complete planned set."}]}, {"description": "The input accounting is internally consistent with the raw data: 40 planned units, 8 removed, 32 retained, 24 confirmed fledging events; the data.csv contains 40 unit rows (NB-01 through NB-40) with 8 rows marked removed and 24 retained rows marked fledging_event=yes.", "observed_value": {"planned": 40, "removed": 8, "retained": 32, "events": 24}, "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "Planned nest boxes: 40\nPrespecified screening step: retain a nest box only if a complete clutch was confirmed on or before 15 May 2025.\nNest boxes removed by screening: 8\nNest boxes retained after screening: 32\nNest boxes with a confirmed fledging event (at least one chick fledged): 24"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "box_id,site,screening_status,removal_reason,fledging_event\nNB-01,Alder Fen,retained,none,yes"}]}, {"description": "The scope notes explicitly state that the 8 screened-out boxes remain inside the denominator and that no retained-subset-only rate is claimed, confirming the claimed quantity's domain and the computation's domain coincide.", "observed_value": "denominator explicitly stated as complete set of 40", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 22, "end_line": 24, "quoted_text": "The denominator of the selected rate is the complete planned set of 40 nest boxes, matching the declared scientific target.\nThe 8 screened-out nest boxes remain inside that denominator; no fledging event was confirmed for any of them.\nNo rate is claimed here for the 32 retained nest boxes alone."}]}, {"description": "The generating script hard-codes RATE_PERCENT = '60.0' alongside PLANNED_UNITS = '40' and FLEDGING_EVENTS = '24', consistent only with a complete-domain denominator of 40.", "observed_value": "60.0 = 24/40", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 10, "quoted_text": "PLANNED_UNITS = '40'\nREMOVED_UNITS = '8'\nRETAINED_UNITS = '32'\nFLEDGING_EVENTS = '24'\nRATE_PERCENT = '60.0'"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "A potential objection: the removed boxes were never assessed for fledging outcomes (fledging_event = not_assessed), so outcome information exists only for the retained subset, and one could argue the numerator is subset-derived. However, the report's claimed quantity is the rate of confirmed fledging events across all 40 planned boxes, its denominator is the complete domain, and the report transparently discloses that no event was confirmed for the screened-out boxes. This does not constitute a subset computation being claimed for the complete domain, which is the specific in-scope issue.", "observed_value": "not_assessed outcomes for removed units, disclosed in the report", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "NB-05,Alder Fen,removed,clutch_never_completed,not_assessed"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "The 8 screened-out nest boxes remain inside that denominator; no fledging event was confirmed for any of them."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to show the reported 60.0 percent was actually computed on the retained subset: 24/32 = 75.0 percent and 24/40 = 60.0 percent, so the reported figure is arithmetically consistent only with the complete-domain denominator of 40. I also tested whether the numerator's reliance on assessments made only among retained boxes could constitute the in-scope issue; the report explicitly defines the quantity as confirmed events over all 40 planned boxes and discloses the not_assessed status of removed boxes, so the claimed quantity's domain matches the computation's domain. Both falsification routes failed, supporting the no-issue verdict.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:5b1bce664dbff4b6f405", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task statement declares the scientific target to be the prespecified eligible subset, not the complete planned set, so the declared target domain is the retained subset itself.", "observed_value": "target domain = prespecified eligible subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the prespecified eligible subset of observation units, with every claim explicitly confined to that subset."}]}, {"description": "The report identifies the 8 retained stations as the scientific target and explicitly confines all claims to that subset.", "observed_value": "claims explicitly confined to retained subset of 8", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "Retained post-screening stations (the scientific target): 8"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 9, "end_line": 9, "quoted_text": "All claims below apply only to the retained subset, not the complete planned set."}]}, {"description": "The selected result claims a rate only for the 8 retained stations, and the arithmetic is exact for that domain: 6/8 = 75.0 percent. The claimed domain and the computed domain coincide; no quantity is claimed for the complete planned set of 10.", "observed_value": "6/8 = 75.0 percent, subset-scoped claim", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 11, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Fox detection rate among the 8 retained stations: 6 of 8, 75.0 percent."}]}, {"description": "The raw data confirms the accounting: 10 planned stations, 2 excluded for camera failure, 8 retained, of which 6 have fox_detected=yes (ST-01, ST-03, ST-05, ST-08, ST-09, ST-10).", "observed_value": {"planned": 10, "excluded": 2, "retained": 8, "detections": 6}, "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "station_id,planned,screening_status,fox_detected\nST-01,yes,retained,yes\nST-02,yes,retained,no\nST-03,yes,retained,yes\nST-04,yes,excluded_camera_failure,not_assessed"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "A potential objection: the report mentions the complete design of 10 planned stations, which could be read as invoking a complete domain. However, this line is descriptive accounting only; the declared scientific target and the selected result are both explicitly the retained subset, so no quantity is claimed for the complete planned set.", "observed_value": "complete design mentioned only as accounting context", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Planned camera-trap stations in the complete design: 10"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to find any claim in the report that attributes a quantity to the complete planned set of 10 stations while computing on the 8 retained stations. The only rate claim in the report is line 11, which is explicitly scoped to the 8 retained stations, and line 9 disclaims applicability to the complete planned set. The arithmetic 6/8 = 75.0 matches the claim's own stated domain. The in-scope issue requires a complete-domain claim backed by a subset computation; no complete-domain claim exists here, so the falsification attempt failed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:ce8220b59efdff3392a3", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The selected result claims a fledging-event rate of 75.0 percent for the complete planned set of 40 nest boxes, but 24 confirmed events out of 40 planned boxes is 60.0 percent; 75.0 percent equals 24/32 exactly, so the reported rate was demonstrably computed over only the 32 retained (post-screening) nest boxes while being attributed to the complete declared target domain of 40 planned boxes.", "root_cause": "The rate was hard-coded as 75.0 percent (24 events divided by the 32 retained boxes remaining after the clutch-completion screening) in the generating script, and the report text attaches that retained-subset rate to the complete planned set of 40 boxes declared as the scientific target, without any disclosed or approved deviation.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report declares the complete planned set of 40 nest boxes as the scientific target.", "observed_value": "target domain = 40 planned boxes", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "The declared scientific target is the complete planned set of 40 monitored nest boxes."}]}, {"description": "The selected result claims 75.0 percent for the complete planned set of 40 boxes based on 24 events. But 24/40 = 60.0 percent, not 75.0 percent, while 24/32 = 75.0 percent exactly, matching the retained-subset denominator disclosed in the same report.", "observed_value": "claimed 75.0 for domain of 40; 24/40 = 60.0; 24/32 = 75.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] The fledging-event rate for the complete planned set of 40 planned nest boxes is 75.0 percent, based on 24 confirmed fledging events."}]}, {"description": "The report's own input accounting supplies the numbers that make the mismatch arithmetically decisive: 40 planned, 8 removed, 32 retained, 24 events. The only denominator among these that yields 75.0 percent with 24 events is the retained subset of 32.", "observed_value": {"planned": 40, "removed": 8, "retained": 32, "events": 24}, "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "Planned nest boxes: 40\nPrespecified screening step: retain a nest box only if a complete clutch was confirmed on or before 15 May 2025.\nNest boxes removed by screening: 8\nNest boxes retained after screening: 32\nNest boxes with a confirmed fledging event (at least one chick fledged): 24"}]}, {"description": "The generating script hard-codes RATE_PERCENT = '75.0' alongside RETAINED_UNITS = '32' and FLEDGING_EVENTS = '24'; 24/32 = 75.0, confirming the rate corresponds to the retained subset, not the planned set of 40 also hard-coded in the same block.", "observed_value": "RATE_PERCENT '75.0' = FLEDGING_EVENTS 24 / RETAINED_UNITS 32", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 10, "quoted_text": "PLANNED_UNITS = '40'\nREMOVED_UNITS = '8'\nRETAINED_UNITS = '32'\nFLEDGING_EVENTS = '24'\nRATE_PERCENT = '75.0'"}]}, {"description": "The raw data confirms the accounting: 40 unit rows with 8 marked removed (fledging_event not_assessed) and 24 retained rows with fledging_event=yes, so no reading of the data yields 30 events out of 40 (which would be needed for a legitimate 75.0 percent over the complete domain).", "observed_value": "data supports 24 events among 32 retained of 40 planned", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "box_id,site,screening_status,removal_reason,fledging_event\nNB-01,Alder Fen,retained,none,yes"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "NB-05,Alder Fen,removed,clutch_never_completed,not_assessed"}]}, {"description": "The report explicitly rules out any approved deviation that might reframe the target domain: no protocol amendment or approved method deviation exists.", "observed_value": "no deviation or amendment disclosed", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment or approved method deviation exists for this analysis."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report's own text asserts the rate applies to the complete planned set and that the count and rate derive from the same records; if taken at face value this would suggest a complete-domain computation. However, this assertion is arithmetically incompatible with the report's own stated numbers (24 events, 40 planned boxes yields 60.0 percent, not 75.0), so the textual assertion cannot rescue the claim.", "observed_value": "textual claim of complete-domain scope contradicted by the report's own arithmetic", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 22, "end_line": 22, "quoted_text": "The fledging-event count and the rate above come from the same 2025 monitoring records listed in the input file."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] The fledging-event rate for the complete planned set of 40 planned nest boxes is 75.0 percent, based on 24 confirmed fledging events."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to construct any reading under which 75.0 percent is a legitimate complete-domain figure: (a) a different event count — but the report and script both fix 24 events, and the CSV contains exactly 24 fledging_event=yes rows, so 30/40 is unavailable; (b) a different planned-set size — but the report, script, and CSV all fix 40 planned units; (c) an approved reframing of the target to the retained subset — but the report states no protocol amendment or approved deviation exists and its selected result explicitly names the complete planned set of 40. Every alternative fails; the only arithmetic source of 75.0 in the visible files is 24 divided by the 32 retained boxes, so the demonstrated-issue verdict survives falsification.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}